Third-party software linked into the PackCraft binary
(full list with versions: Cargo.lock; licences enforced by scripts/check-deps.py)

- lepton_jpeg (Microsoft), Apache-2.0: lossless JPEG recompression.
- brotli, brotli-decompressor (Dropbox), BSD-3-Clause AND MIT: --fast route.
- crc32fast, MIT OR Apache-2.0.
- zip (the zip-rs project), MIT: ZIP reading and writing.
- sevenz-rust2 and lzma-rust2, Apache-2.0: 7z reading and writing, LZMA/LZMA2.
- ppmd-rust, CC0-1.0 OR MIT-0: PPMd for zip and 7z.
- libbz2-rs-sys and bzip2 (the trifectatech pure-Rust port), bzip2-1.0.6 and
  MIT OR Apache-2.0: bzip2 for zip and 7z.
- zlib-rs / miniz_oxide (via flate2), Zlib and MIT OR Apache-2.0: Deflate.
- eframe, egui, egui_extras, egui_glow, winit, glow, glutin (desktop app only),
  MIT OR Apache-2.0.
- Inter font by The Inter Project Authors, OFL-1.1 (assets/fonts/Inter-OFL.txt),
  embedded in packcraft-gui.
- Transitive dependencies under MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD-2/3-Clause, Zlib, 0BSD,
  ISC, BSL-1.0, CC0-1.0, Unlicense and Unicode-3.0, as listed in each crate's metadata.

The context-mixing, arithmetic-coding and audio-prediction code is original,
written from published descriptions of the techniques (logistic mixing, SSE,
sign-sign LMS); no GPL or LGPL source was consulted.

